GT patch 0030: cheaper content checks on the GE thread. The per-draw texture, palette and vertex-cache hashes
used a serial mix per 8 bytes (a fifth of the GE thread in a race); fast_hash_bytes uses four independent
multiply lanes. Within one display list, the hash of the same palette or texture bytes is remembered until the
list ends or a block transfer writes memory (ge_renderer_forget_content_hashes, also called by GT's own list
executor). Only cache keys change: what is drawn is the same.

